<title>USA: Goldman to pay 25 pct bonus to workers.</title>
<headline>Goldman to pay 25 pct bonus to workers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co said it is paying a year-end 25 percent bonus to its employees.</p>
<p>&quot;We are concluding a terrific year with favorable results across the firm...In light of our excellent performance, we are pleased to announce the year-end bonus will be 25 percent,&quot; chairman Jon Corzine and vice chairman Henry Paulson said in a memo to employees, dated November 20.</p>
<p>Goldman said the bonus will be paid to all eligible employees on the payroll as of November 29.</p>
<p>Goldman has about 9,000 employees.</p>
<p>Last year, it paid a 20 percent bonus.</p>
</text>
